.TH WHOAMI "1" "2026-07-28" "BNU 9.11" "BNU Commands"
.SH NAME
whoami \- print effective user name
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B whoami
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" This page is derived from GNU Coreutils documentation.
This page documents BNU, an independent Bun implementation compatible with
GNU Coreutils 9.11.
.PP
Print the user name associated with the current effective user ID.
Same as id \fB\-un\fR.
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/whoami#whoami--help'\fB\-\-help\fP\X'tty: link'
display this help and exit
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/whoami#whoami--version'\fB\-\-version\fP\X'tty: link'
output version information and exit
